# M48 (PLAN_BROWSER_PERF_SECURITY.md §2.20, D82) — rung G: a second uncontended write shape,
# distinct from rung D's single-row `POST /cart/items`. `POST /tickets` writes a `Ticket` row *and*
# a companion `TicketEvent` row synchronously (TicketsService.create → logEvent(CREATED)) — no
# shared resource across VUs (unlike checkout-burst's hot product), so this stays uncontended, just
# with a heavier per-request write cost than rung D's cart-add.
#
# `POST /products/:id/reviews` was considered and rejected as this rung's target: it's both
# rate-limited (RateLimitGuard, 3/window per user+product) *and* `@Unique(['userId','productId'])`
# at the DB level — a fixed load-user/product pool 409s permanently after each pair's first
# success, so a sustained run would measure the uniqueness wall, not write throughput.
#
# `LoadAdminService.reset()` was extended (this milestone) to delete the load user's tickets
# between runs (cascades to ticket_events at the DB level) so this rung stays repeatable — run
# `POST /admin/load/reset` (bearer admin auth) before each run, same as rungs C/D/E.

test "M48 ticket-write" as load
  ramp to 60 users over 20s
  api POST /tickets body { subject: "load test ticket", description: "generated by the M48 ticket-write rung" }
  expect status equals 201
